+# N30 r2 finite engineering continuation (CPU delivery; not released)
+
+Scientific input and every numerical/online/native-audit byte are the accepted debda23 base. Only generic runner/worker administrative routing changes. The previous original and r1 controllers, authorities, results, invalid receipts and all four charges remain immutable. Only the original two valid controls, with 4ce2 source and IDs, enter the logical matrix. The r1 repaired offline diagnostic is never accepted task data.
+
+Exactly ten prospective rows continue original12: one N30 task0 recovery linked to r1 attempt2138c682c5a7, then untouched task1..3 C0/Q0/N30. At most14combined dispatches, two inherited controls, no further retry/resume. A prior retry_of the named r1 failure in ANY iteration forbids a second reservation. Scientific-cell history checks consider only original/r1/r2, preserving independent older cohorts. Mixed r2/r1/original markers fail. Actual r2 worker routes invoke the unchanged N30 CPU native auditor including zero-guided episodes; no CUDA arithmetic proof is added.
+
+Same complete-triple futility and full12 gate: candidate>=3/4 and>=bothcontrols, verified positive guided/parent/active insertion counts. A missing native receipt, status/journal discrepancy, new invalidity or interrupted prefix never promotes. Unknown costs/tokens remain unknown; actual terminal costs are retained even if processing/status fails. Every original3+r1one+new attempt is a distinct charge, with both invalid IDs and source lineages reported. Resource shortfall yields RESOURCE_BUDGET_INCOMPLETE, not numerical failure.
+
+Combined6GPUh includes1445.4208934970666oldseconds and all attributable preparation. State caps remain578/100h, buckets76/262/180/40/20, protected32/12h. New10slots=baseline3/development6/recovery1; full1840seconds must fit both local/global reservations before every dispatch. Root owns current disk>=20GiB at resolved P/artifacts destination, idle fixedGPU7 UUID, runtime/driver/boot/currentCodex-login and source/adoption checks. Artifact attempts stay at P/artifacts/attempts with unique newIDs; control artifacts stay at L.
+
+## Shallow historical read contract
+
+r2 bridge.history(root) reuses only unchanged r1_bridge.history(root), a bounded JSON/error-text parser for the original two receipts and original failure. It does not invoke r1 source/admission validators under a new HEAD. It additionally binds exact r1 closure/457source/plan/result/journal/invalid context/rejected receipt and accepted repair review/463source. Each metadata file<=8MiB; original reader<=64MiB, and the extension prechecks combined unique prior metadata plus extension reads<=64MiB. No evidence.files tensor, runner.log, repair replay, Stage body or recursive runtime/proof is opened. Root process/raw-integrity/classification/online-byte-parity attestation remains explicit. Current old+r1 ledger subset must exactly equal the frozen combined history; later unrelated cohorts may append independently.
+
+Source bridge compares every463base file; only runner and worker admit an exact whole-file reverse patch. All new scripts/tests/docs are included. Imports must originate in the owning source tree. Current runtime, source, provider, resource and budget verification remains on every generic admission. Historical source IDs are never relabeled as the current source.
+
+## Exact root activation API (future root only)
+
+The five disabled JSON templates are envelopes with executable=false and unresolved fields; they are never copied as live authorities. Root fills exact inner payloads after independent source/runtime/history review. No hashes are circular: source manifest first, then bridge, final review, authority, plan, release.
+
+From the final adopted owning W (with W and W/scripts on sys.path), import scripts.qd_ed_final_runner as r, qd_ed_n23_worker as w, qd_ed_n30_r2_bridge as b, qd_ed_n30_r2_contract as c, and qd_ed_n30_r2_prepare as p. APIs:
+
+- source = w.source_record(W, c.source_paths(vars(r))). Must equal delivered source-manifest-execution-v1.json. b.reverse_source(W, source) checks whole-file reversal to debda23.
+- h = c.history(); runtime = c.runtime_ref(h). Recheck h.old_seconds=1445.4208934970666, two imports, four settled old attempts, no old/r1 later events. c.validate_runtime(w.read_ref(runtime), W, vars(r), h) retains lexical alias ownership and all runtime/Stage/GPU bindings.
+- w.atomic_json(c.BRIDGE, b.build(source, runtime, W)). BRIDGE=L/source-history-bridge-v1.json. This performs bounded historical metadata hashing only; root separately confirms no owned controller/worker.
+- FINAL_REVIEW=L/final-source-runtime-review-v1.json: exactly schema n30-r2-source-runtime-review-v1, disposition accepted, source, runtime, protocol=c.ref(c.PROTOCOL), source_bridge=c.ref(c.BRIDGE), new_tensor_preflight=false, no_gpu_release=true. c.final_review(source,runtime,W) verifies it.
